// ============================================================================
//  zm_qol wpnfix donor  -  built by build_wpnfix.bat, loaded FIRST by build_ff.
//
//  Sole purpose: supply the 1911 weapon defs from RETAIL instead of from
//  zone_source\base\mod.ff. The donor's copies name fire aliases that exist
//  nowhere in BO2 (wpn_m1911_*, wpn_mc96_*), so the guns were silent; retail's
//  copies name wpn_1911_*, which every map bank declares and which the user's
//  sound pack replaces. The Linker is first-load-wins, so the only way to beat
//  the donor is to supply the name from a zone loaded ahead of it.
// ============================================================================
>game,T6

weapon,m1911_zm
weapon,m1911_upgraded_zm
weapon,m1911lh_upgraded_zm

//  v2.8.9 - c96_zm IS DELIBERATELY NOT HERE. User report 2026-08-30: the Mauser
//  has the wrong shooting sound on every map except Origins. Retail's c96_zm asks
//  for wpn_1911_fire_plr, and that alias is MAP-DEPENDENT: zmb_tomb points it at
//  wpn_mauser_fire, every other map bank points it at wpn_fnp45_fire_plr - the
//  M1911's shot. Treyarch could share the name because retail never lets the
//  Mauser leave Origins; this mod does. So the fix is the opposite of the 1911's:
//  let zone_source\base\mod.ff keep supplying c96_zm, whose fire aliases are the
//  UNSHARED wpn_mc96_fire_{plr,npc}, and declare that family in mod.all. Measured:
//  the donor's c96_zm differs from retail's in exactly 2 of 2055 fields (the two
//  fire aliases), and its 11-row wpn_mc96_* chain is a rename of retail Origins'
//  wpn_1911_* chain - same payloads, same secondary wiring. No stock bank declares
//  any wpn_mc96_* name, so nothing is shadowed.
